        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: First United States Congress, United States Senate, United States House of Representatives\n- Places: Federal Hall, Congress Hall, New York City, Philadelphia\n- People: George Washington\n- Topics: United States presidency, United States Constitution\n\nFacts:\n- Federal Hall was built in 1700 as New York's City Hall.\n- The First United States Congress consisted of the United States Senate and the United States House of Representatives.\n- The First United States Congress met from March 4, 1789, to March 4, 1791, during the first two years of George Washington's presidency.\n- The First United States Congress first met at Federal Hall in New York City and later met at Congress Hall in Philadelphia.\n- Federal Hall later served as the first capitol building of the United States under the Constitution.\n- Federal Hall was the site of George Washington's inauguration as the first President of the United States under the Constitution.",
